- op: discuss  # 703c
  at: '2026-08-31T05:10:43Z'  # 703c
  by: agent  # 703c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 703c
  clock: 3  # 703c
  nonce: 703c  # 703c
  message: "SATISFIED on merged dev (PR #666), with the sizing this item demanded done\nFIRST and the fix's shape decided BY it rather than around it.\n\nTHE SIZING, which is the item's own \"BEFORE BUILDING\" step. Expanded OTP's\neight kernel level macros across rabbitmq source-to-source and ran the six\ngeneric taint claims, both arms cold on separate XDG_CACHE_HOME dirs with the\n\"No cached results found\" line asserted, canary confirming the arms differ\n(1910 macro sites -> 0; logger: calls 183 -> 2093 = 183+1910):\n\n  host-secret-no-logging     68 -> 138 situations   (93 -> 2028 pairs)\n  the other SIX claims       byte-identical\n  findings_total            972 -> 1088\n\nSo 1,910 macro sites convert to +70 reported situations -- 3.7%. THE ITEM'S\nOWN HYPOTHESIS IS CONFIRMED AND QUANTIFIED: a recall hole that no source\nreaches is worth far less than its size suggests. Its 91%-of-the-logging-\nsurface framing is true of the SOURCE TEXT and not of the OUTPUT.\n\nAND THE ITEM'S OTHER PREDICTION IS NOW DEMONSTRATED RATHER THAN ARGUED. Keyed\non (source, sink, caller) only 7 of the 68 pre-expansion situations survive,\nwhich reads like mass loss; keyed on (source, caller) ALL 68 survive. The 61\nthat \"vanished\" re-root their sink from io:format to logger:*. That is exactly\nthe coincidental coverage the io_lib removal predicted and could not then\nshow. I nearly published the first key's number: the JSON evidence list is\ncapped at _MAX_EVIDENCE_ROWS=100 while evidence_count is not, so my first\ncomparison was 68 full rows against B's first 100 of 138. Re-ran both arms\nwith the cap raised.\n\nPREDICTION CONFIRMED BY AN INDEPENDENT MECHANISM. The source-transform arm\nforecast 138 rows; the shipped analyzer change, run against UNMODIFIED\nrabbitmq, produces the IDENTICAL 138-row set and the same 1088 total. Two\nroutes to one number.\n\nTHE ITEM ASKED WHICH OF (a) OR (b) TO BUILD. The measurement chose (a), and\nnot for the reason the item expected.\n\n  * The item feared (a) is \"a name-based gate with all the incompleteness that\n    implies\". It need not be name-based. A file only receives OTP's macros by\n    including a header named logger.hrl, so the gate is the INCLUDE. Measured\n    across rabbitmq, emqx, ejabberd and vernemq that covers 2267 of 2267\n    sites; the stricter literal include_lib(\"kernel/include/logger.hrl\")\n    covers 2266 and misses ejabberd's mod_invites_register.erl, which reaches\n    kernel's header through ejabberd's OWN same-named one.\n  * A ?LOG_ PREFIX match would have been the real trap: rabbitmq also defines\n    ?LOG_DIR (a directory string), ?LOG_PREFIX (a prefix string) and\n    ?LOG_EXCH_NAME (a binary). Three logging sinks minted from string\n    literals.\n  * (b), the preprocessor, is refused on measured grounds rather than on cost.\n    General function-like macro NAMES are defined in more than one file at\n    5-21% per repository (87 of 693 in emqx, 21 of 124 in ejabberd), so a\n    global name->body map is ambiguous and correct expansion needs per-file\n    include resolution. The eight kernel names have the opposite property:\n    across six erlang repositories they are NEVER redefined. That asymmetry is\n    the whole argument, and it is recorded beside the vocabulary so a ninth\n    entry has to earn the same evidence.\n\nTHE SCOPE IS WIDER THAN THIS ITEM'S TITLE, AND THAT IS FILED HERE RATHER THAN\nLEFT IMPLICIT. The family is PROJECT-LOCAL LOGGING MACROS, of which OTP's is\none member:\n\n  rabbitmq   1910 OTP sites     183 direct logger:\n  vernemq     347 OTP sites       7 direct   (98% -- more extreme than rabbitmq)\n  emqx          7 OTP sites     211 direct   + ?SLOG 1195 / ?SLOG_THROTTLE 38,\n                                               which expand to logger:log\n  ejabberd      3 OTP sites      22 direct   + ?DEBUG/?INFO_MSG/?WARNING_MSG/\n                                               ?ERROR_MSG/?CRITICAL_MSG = 1330,\n                                               which expand to ?LOG_*\n  rebar3/cowboy/proper/recon/pobox: ZERO macro sites\n\nOTP's eight names are 2,267 of roughly 3,530 macro-mediated logging sites --\nabout 64%. The remaining 36% needs the include-resolving expander this change\ndeclines to build, and the module docstring says so rather than implying\ncompleteness. Whether to build it is a separate decision with its own sizing;\nI am not filing a sub-item for it unprompted.\n\nCI CAUGHT A REAL GAP AND I FIXED IT THE STRICT WAY. check-schema-coverage\nflagged `macro_expansion` as a new uncovered canonical value and offered\n--update-baseline. That would have GROWN a shrink-only ratchet -- the\ndirection .ci/mypy-strict-baseline.json forbids -- so instead the corpus\ngained the smallest erlang file that triggers the producer, and the baseline\nSHRANK by one entry (Symbol.kind \"module\", newly covered as a side effect of\nthe corpus gaining its first erlang file). Nothing was added to it.\n\nTests: 18903 passed, 3 skipped, 15 xfailed; 100% coverage on changed sources;\nmypy ratchet clean. Nine tests on the analyzer change, including controls that\nan ungated macro emits nothing, that ?LOG_DIR is not a logging call, that a\ndirect logger: call is unchanged, and that the expanded edge is priced BELOW a\nliteral call measured in the same run rather than against a constant."  # 703c
